  "summary": "Slide 68: heap objects live until you delete them, even when the pointer variable is long gone.",
  "code": "struct Order { int id; double price; };\n\nint main() {\n  int *p{ new int{} };\n  *p = 5;\n  delete p;\n  for (int id = 1; id <= 2; ++id) {\n    Order *o = new Order{ id, 100.0 + id };\n    // forgot: delete o;\n  }\n}",
